  "worked_solution": "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(s) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{4}+10s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(55)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612s,\\,4{s}^{3}+10,\\,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the second derivative by differentiating ${f}^{\u2032}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(s) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4{s}^{3}+10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-4\\operatorname{cos}\u20612s,\\,12{s}^{2},\\,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
